From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:48:42 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: lp855x: report register brightness readback

Without get_brightness the backlight core reports the requested level as
actual_brightness, even while LP8556 BL_CTL is off. This obscures display
blanking diagnostics: the requested level is retained for unblanking and
is not necessarily the level applied to the LEDs.

Read the existing brightness register in register-based mode. LP8556
register-only mode additionally reads BL_CTL and reports zero while it is
disabled. Propagate I2C errors rather than reporting a cached value. PWM
mode retains the effective software level because its clock-backed PWM
provider cannot read the hardware duty cycle.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c b/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c
@@ -262,9 +262,30 @@
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
+static int lp855x_bl_get_brightness(struct backlight_device *bl)
+{
+	struct lp855x *lp = bl_get_data(bl);
+	int ret;
+
+	if (lp->mode == PWM_BASED)
+		return backlight_get_brightness(bl);
+
+	if (lp->chip_id == LP8556 &&
+	    (lp->pdata->device_control & GENMASK(2, 1)) == BIT(2)) {
+		ret = i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(lp->client, LP855X_DEVICE_CTRL);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			return ret;
+		if (!(ret & BIT(0)))
+			return 0;
+	}
+
+	return i2c_smbus_read_byte_data(lp->client, lp->cfg->reg_brightness);
+}
+
 static const struct backlight_ops lp855x_bl_ops = {
 	.options = BL_CORE_SUSPENDRESUME,
 	.update_status = lp855x_bl_update_status,
+	.get_brightness = lp855x_bl_get_brightness,
 };
 
 static int lp855x_backlight_register(struct lp855x *lp)
-- 
